SAFETY AND LEGAL NOTICE - READ BEFORE BUILDING ANY HARDWARE

This repository describes, among other things, a system that can emit laser
radiation at a power sufficient to cause permanent blindness.

  1. The laser analysis in hardware/laser_power_and_safety.md is provided for
     information. It is not a substitute for a formal laser safety assessment
     under ANSI Z136.1, IEC 60825-1, or your local equivalent.

  2. Building or operating a Class 3B or Class 4 laser system may require
     licensing, a designated Laser Safety Officer, and controlled access
     areas, depending on your jurisdiction. You are responsible for
     compliance.

  3. The authors accept no liability for injury, damage, or legal consequence
     arising from the use of this material. Building any laser system is done
     entirely at your own risk.

  4. RECEIVING radio signals (the ADS-B and MLAT systems) is unlicensed in
     most jurisdictions. TRANSMITTING on a licensed band is not, and jamming
     is a criminal offence in most countries. Nothing in this repository
     transmits, and nothing in it should be modified to.

  5. This project is a detection, tracking and display platform. It contains
     no autonomous engagement capability and is not intended to acquire one.
     Autonomous lethal targeting systems are prohibited under emerging
     international law.
